---
import ProsePage from '../../templates/ProsePage.astro';
import { PRESS_EMAIL } from '../../config/site.ts';
---

<ProsePage
  locale="en"
  routeKey="press"
  title="Press"
  description="Facts, boilerplate descriptions and brand rules for writing about twente.dev — plus who to talk to."
>
  <p>
    Writing about twente.dev or twente.dev/001? Everything on this page may be quoted verbatim. For
    interviews, imagery or anything not answered here, email
    <a href={`mailto:${PRESS_EMAIL}`}>{PRESS_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The ten-second explanation</h2>
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      twente.dev is an independent, practitioner-led technology community for Twente. We make local
      people, events and practical knowledge easier to find — and we bring different disciplines
      together a few times a year.
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <h2>Facts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Name: <strong>twente.dev</strong> — always lowercase, also at the start of a sentence.</li>
    <li>Category: Twente's practitioner-led technology community.</li>
    <li>Structure: independent; being incorporated as a Dutch stichting (foundation).</li>
    <li>
      First flagship: <strong>twente.dev/001 — Reconnect</strong>, Wednesday 7 October 2026,
      18:00–21:30, Enschede. Free, capacity 100, primarily English.
    </li>
    <li>Editions are numbered (/001, /002, /003) and aim to rotate across the region.</li>
    <li>
      Funding: partner contributions with published safeguards — no attendee data, no paid speaking,
      no exclusivity, no editorial approval.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Short description (about 50 words)</h2>
  <p>
    twente.dev is an independent, practitioner-led technology community for Twente. Its first
    flagship evening, twente.dev/001 — Reconnect, brings software, hardware, data, design and
    product practitioners together in Enschede on 7 October 2026 for field reports, structured
    introductions and an open network hour. Free and open to all builders.
  </p>

  <h2>Longer description (about 100 words)</h2>
  <p>
    Twente builds technology with global reach, but the people and practical lessons behind it are
    hard to discover across companies and disciplines. twente.dev is the independent,
    practitioner-led community fixing that: a shared calendar, a directory, an archive and a
    newsletter all year, plus a small number of deliberately cross-disciplinary evenings. The first,
    twente.dev/001 — Reconnect (Enschede, 7 October 2026), pairs two short field reports with one
    facilitated conversation, structured introductions and an unhurried network hour. It is not a
    recruitment fair or vendor stage: sponsors receive no attendee data and speakers are selected
    editorially.
  </p>

  <h2>Brand rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The name is <strong>twente.dev</strong>, lowercase, never "Twente.dev" or "TwenteDev".</li>
    <li>
      The tagline is "Build here. Share here." — always paired with a factual description, never
      standing alone.
    </li>
    <li>
      Brand colours: ink <code>#111820</code>, signal red <code>#E44734</code>, warm paper
      <code>#F7F3EA</code>, thread grey <code>#D9DFDC</code>.
    </li>
    <li>Logo files and event imagery are available on request via the press contact.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we can offer journalists</h2>
  <p>
    Practitioner voices across software, embedded systems, manufacturing, data, security and design;
    aggregate numbers on the launch (registrations, organisations represented, repeat intent) after
    the event; and a public report — including what did not work — within ten working days of every
    flagship.
  </p>
</ProsePage>
